    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as our primary offensive engine. With a score of 68.55, he is the clear standout, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Gray. His strong platoon split against right-handed pitching, combined with a premium spot in the three-hole, elevates his floor significantly above the rest of the infield. While **Jackson Merrill** (57.69) faces a tougher test against the elite pitch mix of Gausman, his dynamic platoon edge and positional stability make him our most reliable outfield anchor for this rotation. **Sam Antonacci** (52.32) and **Miguel Vargas** (48.17) provide necessary stability at the top and middle of the order, respectively, though both are slightly hampered by a neutral park factor and the mid-tier skill profile of Brown. \n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved our marginal starters versus those squeezed out by the roster crunch. **Drake Baldwin** (47.26) earns the start at C1, but his score is suppressed by the elite 2.92 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. While he remains in the lineup, we are closely monitoring the impact of his placement; should he shift down from the two-hole, his efficiency score will likely dip below our replacement threshold. On the bench, the absence of stalwarts like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** due to scheduled off-days leaves a massive void in our power categories. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, further thinning our options for late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit appearances. We are keeping a close eye on the remaining depth\u2014specifically **Heliot Ramos**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Coby Mayo**\u2014to see if any late lineup changes elsewhere require a pivot, but for today, we are banking on the high-contact approach of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to carry the weight.",
